# Maintenance

This folder holds the maintenance jobs of the repository and the adapters that run them.

| Path | Content |
|---|---|
| `jobs.yaml` | Manifest: the jobs, the paths each may change and the commit title |
| `jobs/` | One instruction file per job |
{%- if maintain_adapter == 'manual' %}
| `manual/` | Adapter for a local run |
{%- endif %}

## Run

```sh
mise run maintain -- prompt docs-drift
{%- if maintain_adapter == 'manual' %}
.maintain/manual/run docs-drift --local -- <agent command>
{%- else %}
mise run maintain -- run docs-drift --local -- <agent command>
{%- endif %}
```

Jobs: `docs-drift`, `baseline-burndown`, `dead-code`. Every job ends in a pull request from `maintain/<job>`; no job merges or pushes to another branch.

`mise run maintain -- start|publish|run <job> [--local]` is the contract all adapters share. `--local` stops after the commit: no push, no pull request.

## Own adapter

Create `.maintain/<adapter>/` with a `README.md` that states what the folder holds and how to run it, and an executable `run` that calls `mise run maintain -- run <job>`. Record the folder name as the answer `maintain_adapter` in `.repo.yaml`, changed as `AGENTS.md` prescribes.

An adapter that runs `publish` as a separate process after the agent, such as a CI job, runs the code of `.mise/` from a clean checkout of the base branch, with the tree of the agent as the current folder. `run` loads the code before the agent starts, so it needs no such care.

## Limits of the protection

`maintain` reads the manifest and the protected paths from the base branch and stops before any code of the tree runs when a job changes a path outside its list. The limits cover a mistake of an agent and a bypass of the checks through repository files. An agent with an arbitrary shell can change `.git/config` and the environment; the last barrier is CI and the review of the pull request.
